WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.125 --> 00:00:07.541
I just spent an unforgettable 14 days
traveling through South Korea.

00:00:08.208 --> 00:00:11.916
The aim of this trip was to experience the
very best the country had to offer.

00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:14.708
From the vibrant and busy
capital of Seoul,

00:00:15.208 --> 00:00:17.583
to the coastal charms of Busan
with its sandy

00:00:17.625 --> 00:00:19.541
beaches and lively markets.

00:00:20.166 --> 00:00:23.625
And finally, Jeju Island, known for its
breathtaking natural scenery.

00:00:24.833 --> 00:00:26.833
If you're planning to do a similar trip,

00:00:27.125 --> 00:00:29.541
or in search of some inspiration,
then join

00:00:29.583 --> 00:00:32.791
me on this incredible journey through
the heart of South Korea.

00:00:33.333 --> 00:00:36.291
Here's how to spend 14 days
in South Korea.

00:00:47.333 --> 00:00:49.000
Here's a quick overview of the trip.

00:00:54.708 --> 00:00:58.000
We'll begin with 6 days in Seoul, diving
into the heart of the capital.

00:00:58.583 --> 00:01:00.916
Exploring its dynamic districts 
like Myeongdong,

00:01:01.416 --> 00:01:03.916
Hongdae, and Gangnam, 
visiting iconic landmarks

00:01:04.125 --> 00:01:06.875
such as Gyeongbokgung Palace
and N Seoul Tower

00:01:06.875 --> 00:01:09.291
while indulging in its vibrant
culinary scene.

00:01:10.833 --> 00:01:12.666
Next, we head south to Busan.

00:01:14.041 --> 00:01:16.416
We take in the coastal scenery and stroll

00:01:16.416 --> 00:01:19.458
along the sandy beaches of
Haeundae and Gwangalli.

00:01:19.791 --> 00:01:22.416
We visit a cliffside temple
and wander through a 

00:01:22.416 --> 00:01:24.708
historic village and explore
the busy markets.

00:01:28.291 --> 00:01:30.333
And finally, we wrap things up 
on Jeju island,

00:01:30.916 --> 00:01:32.958
renting a car and setting
off on a scenic

00:01:32.958 --> 00:01:34.791
drive around its lush landscapes.

00:01:35.291 --> 00:01:37.416
From waterfalls to volcanic craters,

00:01:37.583 --> 00:01:40.291
we discover the island's natural
wonders at our own pace,

00:01:40.583 --> 00:01:42.958
enjoying a slower rhythm of travel.

00:01:43.916 --> 00:01:46.458
Before we begin, let's get the
basics out of the way.

00:01:46.916 --> 00:01:48.916
The best season to visit South Korea is

00:01:48.916 --> 00:01:51.500
either autumn or spring, as
the weather conditions

00:01:51.583 --> 00:01:53.125
are milder during this time.

00:01:54.208 --> 00:01:55.666
We want to avoid the summer months since

00:01:55.666 --> 00:01:59.041
the country is notorious for
its hot and humid weather

00:01:59.791 --> 00:02:03.708
Winter can be an option to avoid the crowds,
but the temperatures can be freezing.

00:02:04.416 --> 00:02:06.208
South Korea boasts an extensive public

00:02:06.208 --> 00:02:09.125
transportation system, making it
simple to navigate through

00:02:09.125 --> 00:02:09.916
the entire country.

00:02:10.291 --> 00:02:11.875
During our journey, we'll mostly use a

00:02:11.875 --> 00:02:14.916
combination of trains and buses
to get in and around the cities

00:02:15.291 --> 00:02:17.916
For this, the T-Money Travel Card will
be our key to the country.

00:02:18.291 --> 00:02:21.083
It works similarly to other rechargeable
transportation cards.

00:02:21.541 --> 00:02:25.208
It can even be used as a payment form at
selected stores and vending machines.

00:02:25.791 --> 00:02:29.000
During our time in Korea, we also
frequently use local taxis.

00:02:29.708 --> 00:02:31.791
Taxis in South Korea are relatively
affordable.

00:02:32.250 --> 00:02:34.458
We mostly use them when traveling
with large luggage.

00:02:35.041 --> 00:02:37.375
To get a hold on one, we use
the Kakao Taxi app.

00:02:37.666 --> 00:02:39.708
It's fairly simple to use and
especially useful

00:02:39.708 --> 00:02:41.541
if you don't speak Korean,
since you can input

00:02:41.541 --> 00:02:43.875
the destination even before
entering the taxi,

00:02:44.250 --> 00:02:46.500
saving yourself from some 
embarrassing attempts

00:02:46.708 --> 00:02:48.291
at speaking your broken Korean.

00:02:48.500 --> 00:02:50.708
Getting around on foot, we
used a Naver map.

00:02:51.208 --> 00:02:52.541
It's similar to Google Maps, which

00:02:52.541 --> 00:02:55.208
unfortunately doesn't currently
offer walking directions

00:02:55.375 --> 00:02:59.166
in Korea, but it does still show
you your live GPS location.

00:03:00.375 --> 00:03:02.333
Naver Map has an English
interface, but it

00:03:02.333 --> 00:03:04.250
can still be tricky at times
to find specific

00:03:04.250 --> 00:03:08.416
locations as the English translations of
place names can be a bit hit and miss.

00:03:08.833 --> 00:03:11.416
My solution was to switch between
Naver Map and Google Maps.

00:03:11.875 --> 00:03:15.791
I found it easier to search for locations in
Google Maps first, then copy the place

00:03:15.791 --> 00:03:19.416
name or address in Korean and paste it
into Naver Map to get directions.

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:23.416
Here's a list of some essential apps
you should consider using.

00:03:23.833 --> 00:03:26.208
The already mentioned Naver Map
for navigation.

00:03:27.083 --> 00:03:29.666
Papago, a handy translation
app you can use

00:03:29.666 --> 00:03:31.916
to communicate with locals
or translate food

00:03:31.916 --> 00:03:33.416
menus or signs in Korean.

00:03:33.916 --> 00:03:36.625
Kakao Taxi, the best app to use when
you need to get a taxi.

00:03:37.166 --> 00:03:39.625
And CatchTable, a popular
dining reservation

00:03:39.625 --> 00:03:41.708
app that allows you to make
reservations at

00:03:41.708 --> 00:03:43.791
many popular restaurants in South Korea.

00:03:45.208 --> 00:03:47.375
If you want a written version
of all of this,

00:03:47.375 --> 00:03:50.333
then I'm glad to announce
my 14 days in South Korea

00:03:50.333 --> 00:03:52.083
travel guide is now available.

00:03:52.750 --> 00:03:55.583
This plus 280 page guide
is based on my own

00:03:55.583 --> 00:03:57.750
journey through South Korea
covering Seoul,

00:03:58.083 --> 00:03:59.375
Busan and Jeju Island.

00:04:00.541 --> 00:04:02.458
Inside you'll find detailed
insights on where

00:04:02.458 --> 00:04:04.833
to stay, how to get around,
your travel budget

00:04:05.166 --> 00:04:05.875
and much more.

00:04:06.541 --> 00:04:09.375
I've included over 200 hand-picked 
recommendations

00:04:09.375 --> 00:04:10.583
covering activities,

00:04:13.083 --> 00:04:13.958
restaurants,

00:04:16.541 --> 00:04:17.583
and cafes,

00:04:17.875 --> 00:04:19.666
many of which aren't mentioned
in this video.

00:04:20.333 --> 00:04:21.916
And best of all, each one comes with a

00:04:21.916 --> 00:04:25.250
Naver Map link to make navigation
as easy as possible.

00:04:26.083 --> 00:04:27.916
I spent weeks putting this
guide together to

00:04:27.916 --> 00:04:29.958
make it the most helpful
resource for anyone

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:31.583
planning a trip to South Korea.

00:04:32.125 --> 00:04:33.958
So if that's you, then consider
checking it out.

00:04:34.333 --> 00:04:36.458
The guide is now available
on my personal store.

00:04:45.916 --> 00:04:49.250
We begin in Seoul, a sprawling metropolis

00:04:49.500 --> 00:04:51.583
where ancient temples stand
in the shadows

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:53.291
of large skyscrapers.

00:04:54.416 --> 00:04:57.833
This city is a collision of past,
present, and future,

00:04:58.708 --> 00:05:01.583
a place where tradition and innovation
come together

00:05:02.083 --> 00:05:04.041
to create a dynamic cultural hub.

00:05:09.750 --> 00:05:12.750
We arrive in Seoul and stay in the
popular area of Myeongdong.

00:05:16.791 --> 00:05:19.833
This area is famous for its shopping,
Korean skincare,

00:05:20.333 --> 00:05:22.791
cosmetics, and its many street
food stalls.

00:05:23.375 --> 00:05:26.416
Given its commercial appeal
and central location,

00:05:26.958 --> 00:05:28.958
Myeongdong is arguably the
best place to stay

00:05:29.375 --> 00:05:30.333
for first-time visitors.

00:05:31.166 --> 00:05:33.125
We opted to stay at the Lotte Hotel

00:05:33.666 --> 00:05:34.833
due to its prime location,

00:05:35.208 --> 00:05:37.500
which was located right next to
the main shopping area

00:05:37.750 --> 00:05:38.291
of Myeongdong.

00:05:42.250 --> 00:05:43.625
On our first full day in Seoul,

00:05:44.041 --> 00:05:45.958
we kick things off with Itaewon.

00:05:46.416 --> 00:05:49.458
But first, a visit to the
iconic N Seoul Tower,

00:05:50.041 --> 00:05:51.500
also known as Namsan Tower.

00:05:52.250 --> 00:05:54.625
For 40 years, this towering
landmark has stood

00:05:54.625 --> 00:05:58.250
as a symbol of Korea and a key
tourist attraction in the city.

00:05:58.666 --> 00:06:01.375
To get up to the tower, most folks
take the cable car,

00:06:01.708 --> 00:06:03.041
which is a quick and easy ride.

00:06:03.458 --> 00:06:04.541
If you're feeling adventurous,

00:06:05.125 --> 00:06:06.083
you could decide to hike up,

00:06:06.416 --> 00:06:08.291
which takes around 30 to 40 minutes.

00:06:08.583 --> 00:06:10.083
Just brace yourself for a lot of stairs.

00:06:12.041 --> 00:06:13.791
You'll also find hundreds,
if not thousands,

00:06:13.791 --> 00:06:15.291
of love locks near the tower.

00:06:20.916 --> 00:06:22.916
Before leaving, we also decided
to participate

00:06:23.416 --> 00:06:24.458
and bought our very own lock.

00:06:29.916 --> 00:06:32.958
We head down to Itaewon and
visit Rain Report,

00:06:33.458 --> 00:06:34.625
a weather-themed cafe.

00:06:35.333 --> 00:06:38.000
The cafe serves up a variety of
beverages and desserts

00:06:38.291 --> 00:06:39.416
in a sleek, modern setting.

00:06:39.791 --> 00:06:42.333
The interior is dominated by
black design elements

00:06:42.541 --> 00:06:44.625
and multiple screens displaying
rain scenes

00:06:44.625 --> 00:06:48.000
and weather forecast, creating a
newsroom-like atmosphere.

00:06:48.916 --> 00:06:50.500
And outside, you'll find a line of people

00:06:50.750 --> 00:06:52.000
gathering around to snap photos

00:06:52.416 --> 00:06:54.250
of the artificial rainfall display,

00:06:54.250 --> 00:06:55.958
which happens every 15 minutes.

00:06:57.333 --> 00:06:58.625
As for some personal favorites,

00:06:59.000 --> 00:07:00.833
the sesame latte is a must-try,

00:07:01.083 --> 00:07:03.666
and a black cloud cake was
a dessert to die for.

00:07:10.583 --> 00:07:12.208
Post-coffee break, we make our way

00:07:12.208 --> 00:07:13.541
to the Leeum Museum of Art.

00:07:14.250 --> 00:07:16.250
This museum is celebrated for its mix

00:07:16.250 --> 00:07:18.708
of traditional Korean and
contemporary art.

00:07:19.250 --> 00:07:21.375
It comprises three distinct buildings,

00:07:21.375 --> 00:07:23.000
one for traditional Korean art,

00:07:24.250 --> 00:07:25.333
one for modern works,

00:07:25.833 --> 00:07:28.458
and a third dedicated to children's
education.

00:07:54.250 --> 00:07:57.625
For dinner, we dive headfirst
into Korean barbecue

00:07:58.166 --> 00:07:59.166
at the Maple Tree House.

00:08:01.875 --> 00:08:03.166
This Korean barbecue restaurant

00:08:03.333 --> 00:08:05.250
offers a solid selection of meats

00:08:05.666 --> 00:08:07.666
with an upscale, yet cozy atmosphere.

00:08:12.416 --> 00:08:14.125
Just order the classics and pair them

00:08:14.125 --> 00:08:14.958
with a couple of beers

00:08:15.375 --> 00:08:18.041
for a quintessential Korean
barbecue experience.

00:08:24.708 --> 00:08:26.875
Afterwards, we make our way
back to Myeongdong,

00:08:26.875 --> 00:08:28.708
where the streets are busy and lined up

00:08:28.958 --> 00:08:31.333
with street food stalls as far
as the eye can see.

00:08:34.000 --> 00:08:35.083
You can either opt for browsing

00:08:35.083 --> 00:08:37.291
the many Korean skincare
stores in the area,

00:08:37.708 --> 00:08:39.333
or if you've got a little more
room for a snack,

00:08:39.666 --> 00:08:40.916
then hit up the street food stalls.

00:08:41.458 --> 00:08:44.750
There's no shortage of tasty and
creative snacks to try.

00:08:53.583 --> 00:08:54.875
Looking for more things to do?

00:08:55.208 --> 00:08:56.041
Then here's a short list.

00:09:07.000 --> 00:09:10.416
On day two, we spend the entire
day exploring Hongdae,

00:09:10.875 --> 00:09:13.166
named after the nearby Hongik University.

00:09:13.708 --> 00:09:16.541
The area serves as a cultural
entertainment hub,

00:09:16.791 --> 00:09:19.750
especially popular among students
and young adults.

00:09:20.375 --> 00:09:22.875
You'll find plenty of affordable
trendy fashion shops,

00:09:23.291 --> 00:09:26.041
diverse street food offerings, and
live street performances.

00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:29.166
First, we visit this unique urban park

00:09:29.500 --> 00:09:31.375
that offers a refreshing green space

00:09:31.875 --> 00:09:33.375
amidst the bustling city.

00:09:33.958 --> 00:09:36.291
It follows the path of a railway line,

00:09:37.125 --> 00:09:38.916
transforming what was once a railroad

00:09:39.083 --> 00:09:40.750
into a vibrant linear park.

00:09:48.666 --> 00:09:51.541
Next, we explore the main shopping
street of Hongdae.

00:09:53.208 --> 00:09:55.541
You'll find plenty of clothing
stores to explore,

00:09:57.291 --> 00:09:58.458
street food to sample,

00:10:00.166 --> 00:10:01.583
and even a shooting range

00:10:01.750 --> 00:10:03.125
if you're up for testing your skills.

00:10:04.625 --> 00:10:07.083
However, arguably the main attraction
of the area,

00:10:07.500 --> 00:10:10.166
aside from shopping, is the live
street performances.

00:10:10.750 --> 00:10:13.000
At any given moment, the
street comes alive

00:10:13.208 --> 00:10:16.000
as performers showcase everything
from magic tricks

00:10:16.416 --> 00:10:18.250
to high energy K-pop dance shows.

00:10:18.583 --> 00:10:20.875
There is never a dull moment in Hongdae.

00:10:29.166 --> 00:10:31.458
Next, we make a visit to Acorn Caricature.

00:10:36.666 --> 00:10:38.208
Here you'll find a friendly artist

00:10:38.666 --> 00:10:41.333
who will draw a cute caricature
of you on a canvas.

00:10:42.083 --> 00:10:43.833
It's a quirky heartfelt souvenir

00:10:44.125 --> 00:10:46.875
that perfectly captures the spirit
of our time in Hongdae.

00:10:52.708 --> 00:10:54.125
If photos are more your thing,

00:10:54.708 --> 00:10:57.333
then head to this unique photo booth
called Don't Look Up.

00:10:58.000 --> 00:10:59.541
It's a photo booth that
allows you to take

00:10:59.541 --> 00:11:00.791
some interesting images

00:11:01.333 --> 00:11:02.958
from a unique top-down perspective.

00:11:14.333 --> 00:11:15.291
For a coffee break,

00:11:15.708 --> 00:11:17.833
we head to the cafe 
called Shin Lee Doga,

00:11:18.416 --> 00:11:22.125
a picturesque cafe located inside
a renovated hanok.

00:11:23.833 --> 00:11:26.708
Whether you choose to sit inside
or in the open courtyard,

00:11:27.250 --> 00:11:29.958
it's a delightful spot to relax,
take a breather,

00:11:30.416 --> 00:11:32.333
or perhaps snap a few pictures.

00:11:38.291 --> 00:11:39.500
If you're a big Ghibli fan,

00:11:40.083 --> 00:11:43.375
then perhaps you would rather want
to visit the Koriko Cafe,

00:11:43.916 --> 00:11:45.583
a charming and whimsical cafe

00:11:45.875 --> 00:11:48.708
themed after the beloved Studio
Ghibli animated film

00:11:48.958 --> 00:11:50.166
Kiki's Delivery Service.

00:11:50.708 --> 00:11:52.875
If you're a fan of the film
or any Ghibli movie,

00:11:53.125 --> 00:11:54.375
then this is a must-visit.

00:11:54.583 --> 00:11:56.583
The cafe offers beverages and pastries

00:11:56.750 --> 00:11:59.416
inspired by the film, such as
this iced Americano.

00:11:59.750 --> 00:12:02.333
There's also a small souvenir
shop on the ground floor

00:12:02.500 --> 00:12:04.458
selling official Studio Ghibli
merchandise.

00:12:09.000 --> 00:12:11.375
If you're hungry, then I recommend
stopping by

00:12:11.458 --> 00:12:14.333
Oreno Ramen, a Michelin-awarded
ramen shop.

00:12:17.000 --> 00:12:19.875
Get the restaurant's signature
Tori Paitan ramen.

00:12:20.375 --> 00:12:22.583
It's a bowl of noodles with a deeply rich

00:12:22.583 --> 00:12:24.833
and flavorful creamy chicken base.

00:12:29.458 --> 00:12:32.375
It's honestly one of the best
ramens I've ever tried,

00:12:32.500 --> 00:12:35.458
so I highly recommend swinging
by if you got the chance.

00:12:36.083 --> 00:12:36.583
Very good.

00:12:36.958 --> 00:12:38.750
I'm surprised.

00:12:39.000 --> 00:12:41.250
Usually you think ramen, you think Japan,

00:12:41.625 --> 00:12:45.291
but I honestly think they do
pretty decent effort here.

00:12:45.333 --> 00:12:46.250
It's really good.

00:12:47.541 --> 00:12:50.708
For more things to do in Hongdae,
consider the following.

00:13:04.208 --> 00:13:07.041
On day three, we visit the 
Bukchon Hanok Village.

00:13:10.000 --> 00:13:11.583
A charming historic district

00:13:11.958 --> 00:13:14.416
known for its well-preserved traditional
Korean houses,

00:13:14.875 --> 00:13:18.916
also known as Hanok's, which dates
back to the Joseon Dynasty.

00:13:19.500 --> 00:13:21.583
Wandering through the narrow
and winding alleyways

00:13:21.583 --> 00:13:23.958
of the Hanok Village, visitors
can experience

00:13:23.958 --> 00:13:25.583
a slice of Korea's past.

00:13:26.625 --> 00:13:28.708
Many of the beautifully restored Hanok's

00:13:28.708 --> 00:13:32.000
now serve as accommodations,
cafes, tea houses,

00:13:32.625 --> 00:13:33.333
and small workshops.

00:13:42.958 --> 00:13:45.375
We make a quick stop at a 
New Balance sneaker shop,

00:13:45.666 --> 00:13:47.458
which is located inside yet another

00:13:47.458 --> 00:13:48.833
beautifully restored Hanok.

00:13:51.750 --> 00:13:53.000
After browsing a few items,

00:13:53.583 --> 00:13:55.708
I decided to pick up a new pair of shoes.

00:13:59.750 --> 00:14:01.666
After some exploring, it's
time for a break

00:14:02.000 --> 00:14:04.291
to stay in tune with the ongoing
Hanok theme.

00:14:04.500 --> 00:14:06.958
We visit Onion Cafe, a popular cafe

00:14:07.333 --> 00:14:08.875
housed in a renovated Hanok.

00:14:09.541 --> 00:14:12.125
The cafe features an impressive
selection of pastries

00:14:12.125 --> 00:14:14.250
and baked goods all made in-house.

00:14:20.125 --> 00:14:22.541
We decided to pick up a couple
of interesting items

00:14:23.500 --> 00:14:25.041
along with their signature goods.

00:14:34.166 --> 00:14:35.500
How is it?

00:14:37.791 --> 00:14:38.750
Good. Sweet.

00:14:39.666 --> 00:14:42.791
After refueling, we make our way
to Gyeongbokgung Palace,

00:14:43.125 --> 00:14:44.666
one of South Korea's most iconic

00:14:44.916 --> 00:14:46.958
and historically significant landmarks.

00:14:47.458 --> 00:14:50.083
Built in 1395 during the Joseon Dynasty,

00:14:50.416 --> 00:14:52.333
it served as the main royal palace.

00:14:52.875 --> 00:14:54.458
The palace complex is vast.

00:14:54.916 --> 00:14:57.083
Showcasing traditional Korean
architecture,

00:14:57.750 --> 00:14:59.958
about one third of the original
500 buildings

00:14:59.958 --> 00:15:02.125
have been restored, though many were lost

00:15:02.291 --> 00:15:04.458
or damaged during times of war.

00:15:12.375 --> 00:15:14.708
We were lucky enough to experience
the palace after dark,

00:15:15.041 --> 00:15:17.875
which gave it an almost magical
and mysterious vibe.

00:15:21.583 --> 00:15:23.208
The night event is usually held

00:15:23.208 --> 00:15:25.458
for a limited time during
spring and autumn,

00:15:25.750 --> 00:15:27.666
so make sure the purchase
your tickets in advance

00:15:28.000 --> 00:15:29.041
if you're interested in visiting.

00:15:38.291 --> 00:15:39.833
In the evening, I highly recommend

00:15:40.000 --> 00:15:41.250
strolling through the Hanok village

00:15:41.750 --> 00:15:43.833
once the crowds have thinned out.

00:15:47.875 --> 00:15:50.000
Looking for more things to do,
here's a short list.

00:16:00.416 --> 00:16:02.333
On day four, we head to Gangnam.

00:16:04.500 --> 00:16:06.500
But before that, grab some
morning noodles

00:16:06.916 --> 00:16:08.541
at the famous Myeongdong Kyoja.

00:16:09.250 --> 00:16:12.583
It's so stable since 1966,
Myeongdong Kyoja

00:16:13.041 --> 00:16:15.500
is famous for its hand-cut
kalguksu noodles

00:16:16.000 --> 00:16:17.833
served in a rich chicken broth.

00:16:19.625 --> 00:16:21.458
Do also make sure to order a round

00:16:21.458 --> 00:16:22.625
of their signature dumplings.

00:16:33.541 --> 00:16:35.875
After a satisfying meal,
we head to Gangnam

00:16:36.541 --> 00:16:38.750
and start the day at the
Bonguensa Temple.

00:16:39.166 --> 00:16:41.750
The temple itself has undergone
numerous renovations

00:16:42.166 --> 00:16:44.166
and reconstructions over the centuries.

00:16:44.708 --> 00:16:47.250
It's known for being a beautiful
and quiet sanctuary,

00:16:47.791 --> 00:16:49.625
amidst Seoul's busy Gangnam district.

00:16:50.791 --> 00:16:52.916
The highlight of the temple
is the tall statue

00:16:52.916 --> 00:16:55.666
of the future Buddha, one of the
tallest stone statues

00:16:55.666 --> 00:16:56.458
in the country.

00:16:58.625 --> 00:17:00.125
Next, we head to COEX Mall

00:17:00.666 --> 00:17:02.041
and visit the Starfield Library.

00:17:02.916 --> 00:17:05.458
Known for its design featuring
towering bookshelves

00:17:05.458 --> 00:17:06.708
that reach up to 13 meters,

00:17:07.375 --> 00:17:09.791
the library houses approximately
50,000 books

00:17:09.791 --> 00:17:11.375
and 600 types of magazines,

00:17:11.833 --> 00:17:13.041
with numerous seating areas,

00:17:13.250 --> 00:17:15.333
from cozy nooks to communal tables.

00:17:15.875 --> 00:17:17.666
However, most tourists come
here for the photos

00:17:17.666 --> 00:17:18.625
by the escalator.

00:17:23.916 --> 00:17:26.541
You'll find plenty of shopping
opportunities at COEX,

00:17:26.541 --> 00:17:28.208
as well as the COEX Aquarium,

00:17:28.208 --> 00:17:29.833
which we also decided to visit.

00:17:35.583 --> 00:17:37.625
This impressive indoor oceanic world

00:17:37.625 --> 00:17:40.000
is home to over 40,000 marine creatures

00:17:40.541 --> 00:17:42.625
across roughly 650 species,

00:17:42.916 --> 00:17:45.083
displayed in 14 themed zones.

00:17:50.833 --> 00:17:52.125
Next, we head to Apgujeong,

00:17:52.541 --> 00:17:54.833
an upscale neighborhood filled
with flagship stores,

00:17:55.083 --> 00:17:57.250
designer boutiques, and luxury brands.

00:17:58.000 --> 00:17:59.791
Here are a few of the stores we visited.

00:18:00.416 --> 00:18:03.208
Ader Eror, a streetwear brand
with a cult following.

00:18:03.458 --> 00:18:06.750
Blends bold designs with playful
deconstructed aesthetics.

00:18:08.250 --> 00:18:11.250
Its flagship store in Apgujeong
is a visual treat

00:18:11.708 --> 00:18:14.333
and is more like an art exhibition
than a retail store.

00:18:15.166 --> 00:18:16.083
It's worth coming by,

00:18:16.083 --> 00:18:17.541
even if you don't plan to
do any shopping.

00:18:23.500 --> 00:18:25.333
Tambourines is a Korean fragrance brand

00:18:25.333 --> 00:18:26.791
known for its minimalist aesthetics

00:18:27.375 --> 00:18:28.958
and artistic approach to scent.

00:18:29.458 --> 00:18:31.958
Blending high-quality ingredients
with innovative design,

00:18:32.458 --> 00:18:35.166
the brand creates unique perfumes
and hand-care products.

00:18:38.375 --> 00:18:40.541
Gentle Monster is a Korean eyewear brand

00:18:40.791 --> 00:18:44.125
celebrated for its bold designs and
immersive retail spaces.

00:18:46.666 --> 00:18:50.166
InstantFunk is a Seoul-borne unisex,
casual fashion label,

00:18:50.583 --> 00:18:52.916
defined by its playful mix
of vintage nostalgia

00:18:53.375 --> 00:18:54.666
and contemporary cool.

00:18:58.375 --> 00:19:00.958
Worksout is a high-end streetwear
retailer,

00:19:01.250 --> 00:19:03.583
housed in a striking, three-story
building,

00:19:03.958 --> 00:19:05.875
it offers an expansive gallery-like space

00:19:05.958 --> 00:19:07.875
filled with over 40 curated brands.

00:19:09.541 --> 00:19:11.708
Located in the trendy Do San Park area,

00:19:12.291 --> 00:19:16.166
Nudake offers a unique fusion of art
and culinary innovation.

00:19:16.625 --> 00:19:18.458
As a concept cafe by Gentle Monster,

00:19:18.958 --> 00:19:20.375
it specializes in pastries

00:19:20.625 --> 00:19:22.208
that look almost too stunning to eat.

00:19:23.166 --> 00:19:24.875
Each dessert is a creative experiment,

00:19:25.375 --> 00:19:29.041
pushing the boundaries of what cakes
and pastries can be.

00:19:34.291 --> 00:19:36.958
As evening arrives, we make our
final stop of the day

00:19:37.375 --> 00:19:39.791
at the Banpo Bridge for the
Rainbow Fountain Show.

00:19:40.416 --> 00:19:42.833
Known as the longest bridge
fountain in the world,

00:19:43.208 --> 00:19:45.166
equipped with over 200 LED lights,

00:19:45.666 --> 00:19:48.208
the fountain creates a vibrant,
colorful water display

00:19:48.458 --> 00:19:49.625
synchronized with music.

00:20:04.375 --> 00:20:05.833
The shows run multiple times a day,

00:20:06.041 --> 00:20:08.083
with each display lasting
around 20 minutes.

00:20:08.541 --> 00:20:10.500
You'll also find many food
stalls by the bridge,

00:20:10.833 --> 00:20:12.208
so it's the perfect place to hang out,

00:20:12.500 --> 00:20:14.833
grab a snack, while enjoying the scenery.

00:20:29.375 --> 00:20:33.458
On our fifth day, we head to Ikseongdong, 
a charming Hanok village.

00:20:37.791 --> 00:20:41.333
The morning started off with rain, which did
give the area an interesting vibe.

00:20:42.041 --> 00:20:43.708
However, the weather quickly dried up.

00:20:45.333 --> 00:20:49.000
This charming labyrinth of narrow alleyways
is a delightful mix of old and new.

00:20:49.708 --> 00:20:51.333
Traditional Hanok houses reimagine as

00:20:51.333 --> 00:20:54.791
small boutiques, cozy tea houses,
and aesthetic cafes

00:20:55.000 --> 00:20:56.041
It's a kind of place where you can lose

00:20:56.041 --> 00:20:58.416
track of time simply by wandering
around and

00:20:58.416 --> 00:20:59.458
soaking in the atmosphere.

00:21:00.791 --> 00:21:02.958
As for a cafe recommendation,
one stand-out

00:21:02.958 --> 00:21:05.666
is Cheongsudang, a beautiful
Hanok style cafe

00:21:05.666 --> 00:21:09.916
with a garden theme that almost feels like
stepping into a Studio Ghibli film.

00:21:13.375 --> 00:21:15.250
Their most popular items
are the traditional

00:21:15.250 --> 00:21:16.458
yakwa desserts,

00:21:17.333 --> 00:21:19.958
and their made
to order souffle castella cake

00:21:24.208 --> 00:21:27.916
For a different option, consider visiting the
Soha Salt Pond Cafe,

00:21:28.458 --> 00:21:30.833
 known for its unique 
salt-infused baked goods.

00:21:31.291 --> 00:21:33.583
Their signature saltbread,
a soft and fluffy

00:21:33.583 --> 00:21:37.250
bun with a subtle salty sweetness,
has become a local favorite.

00:21:41.291 --> 00:21:43.625
Next, we walk down to 
the Cheongyecheon stream,

00:21:43.958 --> 00:21:46.708
an 11-kilometer-long
restored waterway that

00:21:46.708 --> 00:21:48.000
flows through the heart of the city.

00:21:56.958 --> 00:22:01.125
This urban waterway is a testament to
Seoul's dedication to green spaces.

00:22:01.750 --> 00:22:03.625
Even spot fish darting through
the water and

00:22:05.833 --> 00:22:07.833
and hop across stepping stones
that connect the

00:22:07.833 --> 00:22:09.083
two sides of the stream.

00:22:28.583 --> 00:22:30.958
As we follow along the stream,
we eventually

00:22:30.958 --> 00:22:34.125
reach Gwangjang Market, one
of Seoul's oldest

00:22:34.291 --> 00:22:35.750
and largest traditional markets.

00:22:37.833 --> 00:22:41.666
It's the perfect place to dive into the
vibrant culinary world of South Korea.

00:22:42.208 --> 00:22:44.416
The market is lined with food stalls and

00:22:44.416 --> 00:22:47.708
restaurants dishing out every
imaginable Korean food.

00:22:52.208 --> 00:22:54.375
Lisa decided to try some 
mung bean pancakes,

00:22:54.375 --> 00:22:57.541
a crispy Korean savory pancake
made from ground

00:22:57.666 --> 00:22:59.083
mung beans and vegetables.

00:22:59.666 --> 00:23:02.000
Mung bean pancakes

00:23:06.208 --> 00:23:07.416
How is it? 

00:23:08.291 --> 00:23:09.875
Do you like it?

00:23:10.958 --> 00:23:12.583
We also decided to try these fish-shaped

00:23:12.583 --> 00:23:15.000
cakes that comes with 
different fillings

00:23:15.000 --> 00:23:17.500
like red bean paste and custard cream.

00:23:28.125 --> 00:23:30.041
We also couldn't resist the
kalguksu

00:23:30.041 --> 00:23:33.125
from the renowned knife cut noodle
lady of Netflix fame,

00:23:33.458 --> 00:23:36.375
an unmissable experience
for any food enthusiast.

00:23:39.500 --> 00:23:41.458
Observing her as she expertly
hand cuts the

00:23:41.458 --> 00:23:43.625
noodles for each bowl is
just as memorable

00:23:43.708 --> 00:23:44.875
as tasting it.

00:23:48.375 --> 00:23:50.375
When a bowl comes scorching
hot, the broth

00:23:50.375 --> 00:23:53.416
is clear, rich in umami,
and the noodles are

00:23:53.416 --> 00:23:54.458
thick and chewy.

00:24:01.708 --> 00:24:02.875
It's really hot.

00:24:03.250 --> 00:24:04.416
It's okay.

00:24:04.666 --> 00:24:06.875
The noodles are really thick.

00:24:07.750 --> 00:24:10.208
Nowadays it's a very popular place, but I

00:24:10.208 --> 00:24:12.041
would say it's still worth
experiencing if

00:24:12.083 --> 00:24:13.875
you're anywhere near Gwangjang Market.

00:24:22.416 --> 00:24:25.250
Next we make our way to 
Dongdaemun Design Plaza.

00:24:28.500 --> 00:24:30.958
Dongdaemun Design Plaza,
also known as DDP,

00:24:31.250 --> 00:24:34.291
is a multicultural complex
and architectural landmark.

00:24:35.250 --> 00:24:38.833
It stands out for its futuristic design
and multi-functional space.

00:24:39.583 --> 00:24:41.375
The complex supports and
spreads the culture

00:24:41.375 --> 00:24:44.333
and development of design
and fashion in South Korea.

00:24:44.750 --> 00:24:47.166
It hosts various cultural
events, including

00:24:47.166 --> 00:24:50.250
exhibitions, fashion shows,
and conferences.

00:24:56.250 --> 00:24:58.500
Not far from DDP, you'll
find the DOOTA Mall,

00:24:58.750 --> 00:25:00.500
which beckons with its eight
floors of fashion

00:25:00.666 --> 00:25:01.375
and brand stores.

00:25:02.416 --> 00:25:04.750
Open until midnight is the
perfect place for

00:25:04.750 --> 00:25:07.083
those late night shopping urges,
whether you're

00:25:07.125 --> 00:25:10.541
hunting for latest trends or just want to
indulge in some retail therapy.

00:25:13.416 --> 00:25:16.416
For dinner, we return to Ikseongdong
for a dinner reservation

00:25:16.416 --> 00:25:18.791
at Oncheonjip, a
shabu-shabu restaurant

00:25:19.041 --> 00:25:22.375
housed in a restored hanok with a small
open courtyard in the center.

00:25:25.125 --> 00:25:28.208
We ordered the Korean beef set for two
and found the meal delicious.

00:25:29.875 --> 00:25:32.333
I personally enjoy these 
cook-it-yourself experiences

00:25:32.666 --> 00:25:35.208
as they remind me of dining 
at home with the family.

00:25:43.791 --> 00:25:46.375
For more things to do around the
area, here's a short list.

00:25:59.166 --> 00:26:02.125
For our final day in Seoul, 
we spend the day in Seongsu,

00:26:02.416 --> 00:26:04.791
a vibrant up-and-coming 
neighborhood in Seoul.

00:26:05.416 --> 00:26:07.291
Often referred to as the
Brooklyn of Seoul,

00:26:07.750 --> 00:26:11.041
Seongsu has transformed from a
primarily industrial area

00:26:11.041 --> 00:26:12.583
into a trendy artistic district, 

00:26:12.583 --> 00:26:16.041
blending its industrial heritage 
with modern and artistic flair.

00:26:18.625 --> 00:26:20.750
Our day kicks off with a
bagel pilgrimage to

00:26:20.750 --> 00:26:23.750
to Kokkili Bagel, 
also known as Elephant Bagel.

00:26:23.875 --> 00:26:26.125
This two-store gem is a haven
for bagel lovers.

00:26:26.416 --> 00:26:28.875
On the ground floor, you can watch 
the staff whip up an impressive

00:26:28.875 --> 00:26:30.958
array of bagels, while the second floor

00:26:30.958 --> 00:26:32.791
offers plenty of seating spots.

00:26:34.625 --> 00:26:35.833
Whether you're in the mood for a classic

00:26:35.833 --> 00:26:37.416
or something more adventurous, 

00:26:37.750 --> 00:26:39.958
there's a bagel here 
to match your craving.

00:26:42.041 --> 00:26:45.166
Seongsu is a treasure trove 
of unique shopping experiences.

00:26:45.583 --> 00:26:46.708
Here are the following standouts.

00:26:48.333 --> 00:26:50.250
Standoil is a contemporary bag brand,

00:26:50.708 --> 00:26:52.916
known for its sleek designs
and everyday versatility.

00:26:56.500 --> 00:27:00.875
The ADER ERROR store in Seongsu is an
extension of the band's creative universe.

00:27:01.208 --> 00:27:02.958
Designed with ADER ERROR 
signature aesthetics

00:27:02.958 --> 00:27:05.583
the store blurs the line 
between fashion and art.

00:27:08.166 --> 00:27:10.333
BALBAL Vintage is a hidden gem for those

00:27:10.333 --> 00:27:12.166
who love timeless fashion with character.

00:27:12.541 --> 00:27:14.791
With a mix of rare finds and classic pieces

00:27:14.791 --> 00:27:18.250
the store offers a unique selection of vintage
clothing and accessories.

00:27:18.541 --> 00:27:20.416
EQL is a fashion concept store that

00:27:20.416 --> 00:27:21.916
brings together emerging designers,

00:27:21.958 --> 00:27:23.916
streetwear, and contemporary trends,

00:27:24.250 --> 00:27:26.000
in a carefully curated space.

00:27:26.583 --> 00:27:28.541
The Dior store in Seongsu is a striking

00:27:28.541 --> 00:27:30.083
blend of luxury and innovation.

00:27:30.500 --> 00:27:32.416
Housed in a modern 
architectural masterpiece

00:27:32.416 --> 00:27:34.958
the space reinterprets the brand's 
timeless elegance

00:27:34.958 --> 00:27:36.250
with a contemporary edge.

00:27:38.083 --> 00:27:39.166
For a quick coffee break,

00:27:39.166 --> 00:27:40.625
we visit OUDE Bakery.

00:27:40.791 --> 00:27:42.875
This minimalist bakery cafe housed in a

00:27:42.875 --> 00:27:45.375
standalone factory building is
renown for its delectable

00:27:45.416 --> 00:27:48.083
pastries which have become a favorite
among visitors.

00:27:53.750 --> 00:27:55.875
Next we arrive at the Seoul Forest Park.

00:27:58.250 --> 00:28:00.000
This sprawling green space was once a

00:28:00.000 --> 00:28:02.541
water treatment facility now
transformed into a

00:28:02.541 --> 00:28:04.125
multi-purpose urban park.

00:28:04.666 --> 00:28:06.458
The park features lush walking paths,

00:28:06.791 --> 00:28:08.750
bike rentals, flower gardens,

00:28:10.916 --> 00:28:12.458
wildlife you can feed,

00:28:14.750 --> 00:28:17.083
and interactive art installations.

00:28:18.208 --> 00:28:21.250
Overall, it's a place that is both popular
amongst families

00:28:22.875 --> 00:28:23.916
and couples.

00:28:28.291 --> 00:28:30.791
For our final meal in Seoul, 
we head to Mongtan.

00:28:31.375 --> 00:28:33.000
Located in the back streets of Yongsan.

00:28:33.583 --> 00:28:37.250
Mongtan has earned a cult following 
with expertly grilled meats.

00:28:37.750 --> 00:28:40.458
The restaurant is best known 
for its boneless short ribs

00:28:40.458 --> 00:28:42.750
that undergoes a dry aging process, 

00:28:43.166 --> 00:28:45.375
then first seared over 
traditional straw fire,

00:28:45.666 --> 00:28:47.291
with the ribs then 
brought to the table

00:28:47.291 --> 00:28:49.416
and grilled further 
on a hot iron lid.

00:29:04.458 --> 00:29:06.916
Your bite is rich, smoky, and
deeply satisfying.

00:29:07.958 --> 00:29:11.583
Every meal is then finished off with
the optional kimchi fried rice.

00:29:13.958 --> 00:29:15.875
Overall, an elevated take on Korean

00:29:15.875 --> 00:29:18.583
barbecue that still feels grounded
in tradition.

00:29:23.041 --> 00:29:24.708
If you're looking for 
something different to do

00:29:24.708 --> 00:29:28.083
then consider doing some hiking in
Bukhansan National Park,

00:29:28.500 --> 00:29:30.458
for example, the hike to Baegundae Peak.

00:29:32.041 --> 00:29:34.958
If hiking isn't your thing, then here
are some different options.

00:29:45.000 --> 00:29:49.083
As our time in Seoul ends, we make the
journey down south to Busan.

00:29:52.916 --> 00:29:55.791
Our journey to Busan starts
from Seoul Station.

00:30:02.500 --> 00:30:04.875
We decided to take the KTX
train to Busan.

00:30:11.791 --> 00:30:14.916
From Seoul, it takes a little over
2 hours to reach Busan.

00:30:21.250 --> 00:30:24.833
These areas are arguably the best place
to stay while exploring Busan.

00:30:26.500 --> 00:30:28.708
The first being Seomyeon.

00:30:28.916 --> 00:30:31.208
Seomyeon is a busy downtown area, 

00:30:31.375 --> 00:30:34.166
mostly known for its shopping, 
food, and nightlife.

00:30:35.000 --> 00:30:36.750
Thanks to its central location,

00:30:36.958 --> 00:30:38.833
it's arguably the best place to stay 

00:30:39.041 --> 00:30:40.833
if you intend to explore the whole city.

00:30:43.208 --> 00:30:44.833
Next is Haeundae. 

00:30:45.708 --> 00:30:48.416
Haeundae is Busan's 
most famous beach. 

00:30:48.625 --> 00:30:52.625
Here you'll find 5-star hotels, 
soft sand, ocean views,

00:30:52.833 --> 00:30:54.291
and a lively atmosphere.

00:30:55.000 --> 00:30:58.250
It's a little further out, so you do need
to factor in some travel time, 

00:30:58.500 --> 00:31:00.375
but it's an excellent place to relax,

00:31:00.375 --> 00:31:03.250
and get that essential 
Busan beach experience.

00:31:05.833 --> 00:31:08.083
Next to Haeundae, 
you'll find Gwangalli.

00:31:09.666 --> 00:31:11.875
Gwangalli is a popular seaside area,

00:31:12.166 --> 00:31:13.666
especially amongst locals. 

00:31:14.041 --> 00:31:16.250
Famous for its stunning views 
of the Gwangan bridge,

00:31:16.833 --> 00:31:18.708
it's less crowded than Haeundae

00:31:18.708 --> 00:31:20.791
but just as pretty and full of life.

00:31:21.375 --> 00:31:24.708
It's slightly closer to the central part
of the city, but not by much.

00:31:29.041 --> 00:31:31.291
And finally, we have Nampo.

00:31:32.125 --> 00:31:35.166
Nampo-dong is the old 
downtown area of Busan.

00:31:35.750 --> 00:31:37.541
Here you'll find many traditional markets

00:31:37.833 --> 00:31:38.625
street food,

00:31:39.500 --> 00:31:42.541
and of course, the famous 
Jagalchi fish market.

00:31:44.541 --> 00:31:46.125
It's the place to stay if you want to

00:31:46.125 --> 00:31:48.666
experience a bit of the old side of Busan.

00:31:50.625 --> 00:31:53.583
For our time in Busan, 
we decided to stay in Gwangalli.

00:31:55.125 --> 00:31:56.541
We stayed at this lovely accommodation

00:31:56.541 --> 00:31:59.250
which provided an amazing view 
of the nearby bridge.

00:32:00.375 --> 00:32:01.666
The place had more than enough room for

00:32:01.666 --> 00:32:04.500
the both of us, and can easily
fit a group of people.

00:32:05.333 --> 00:32:07.416
The space overall was tastefully
decorated,

00:32:07.791 --> 00:32:09.666
it featured a bath in the living space, 

00:32:11.458 --> 00:32:13.375
and a fully functioning kitchen.

00:32:14.750 --> 00:32:16.708
We really enjoyed staying in, just

00:32:16.708 --> 00:32:19.541
relaxing and taking in the beautiful
night view of

00:32:19.583 --> 00:32:21.083
the lit up Gwangan bridge.

00:32:24.916 --> 00:32:28.375
On our first day in Busan, 
we head to Nampo-dong 

00:32:28.833 --> 00:32:31.958
and visited the famous
Jagalchi market,

00:32:32.208 --> 00:32:35.333
one of Korea's largest and 
most famous seafood markets.

00:32:40.791 --> 00:32:44.625
Jagalchi is regarded as the beating heart 
of the city's seafood scene

00:32:44.916 --> 00:32:47.166
walkng through the market 
you're enveloped in a sensory

00:32:47.166 --> 00:32:50.000
overload of sights, sounds, and smells.

00:32:51.000 --> 00:32:52.791
This isn't simply just a market,

00:32:52.791 --> 00:32:54.750
it's a testament to 
the city's resilience

00:32:54.875 --> 00:32:56.708
and deep connection to the sea

00:33:00.125 --> 00:33:02.666
Alright, so we are in Jagalchi market

00:33:02.666 --> 00:33:05.750
we just spent half an hour walking around

00:33:05.750 --> 00:33:07.708
downstairs where you see all these

00:33:07.708 --> 00:33:09.500
different fish vendors.

00:33:09.916 --> 00:33:11.750
And then after just checking things out,

00:33:11.750 --> 00:33:13.583
we started upstairs where you can find

00:33:13.583 --> 00:33:15.375
the restaurants and this is where you

00:33:15.375 --> 00:33:18.416
can just go in and order

00:33:18.416 --> 00:33:20.416
through like a normal menu basically.

00:33:21.000 --> 00:33:23.250
But you could also go downstairs and buy

00:33:23.250 --> 00:33:26.500
the fish and then bring it up and have

00:33:26.500 --> 00:33:27.958
these different restaurants cook it for you.

00:33:27.958 --> 00:33:30.291
Now if you do that, obviously

00:33:30.291 --> 00:33:31.875
it costs a little bit extra

00:33:31.875 --> 00:33:33.083
to prepare the food, etc.

00:33:33.750 --> 00:33:36.000
But if you don't know what you want and

00:33:36.000 --> 00:33:38.041
you don't know like how the fish is going

00:33:38.041 --> 00:33:40.541
to come out, I recommend just going up to

00:33:40.541 --> 00:33:41.458
the second floor, that's

00:33:41.458 --> 00:33:42.375
where all the restaurants are.

00:33:42.708 --> 00:33:43.916
You see a menu, you can

00:33:43.916 --> 00:33:44.750
pick out what you want.

00:33:44.750 --> 00:33:46.916
It's a little bit cheaper, but of course

00:33:46.916 --> 00:33:48.541
you don't get that experience of picking

00:33:48.541 --> 00:33:50.250
the individual fish or

00:33:50.250 --> 00:33:51.208
shellfish that you want.

00:33:51.625 --> 00:33:53.291
But me and Lisa just decided to head up

00:33:53.291 --> 00:33:57.000
and just look at the menu and pick out

00:33:57.000 --> 00:33:59.041
whatever we felt like.

00:33:59.041 --> 00:34:00.625
We just want to taste a little bit of

00:34:00.625 --> 00:34:01.583
everything, a little bit of

00:34:01.583 --> 00:34:02.458
clams, a little bit of fish.

00:34:02.750 --> 00:34:06.291
Lisa's been dying to try 
a seafood pancake

00:34:06.291 --> 00:34:08.416
 so let's check it out.

00:34:15.375 --> 00:34:16.083
Is it worth it?

00:34:16.666 --> 00:34:17.333
Is it worth it?

00:34:17.416 --> 00:34:17.916
Yes.

00:34:18.666 --> 00:34:20.291
We also ordered some sashimi

00:34:21.208 --> 00:34:22.458
and a couple of shellfish.

00:34:28.958 --> 00:34:31.833
Oh yeah, oh yeah.

00:34:35.791 --> 00:34:37.541
After Jagalchi, we made our way to

00:34:37.666 --> 00:34:40.625
nearby Biff Square, the beating
heart of the Busan

00:34:40.750 --> 00:34:42.083
International Film Festival.

00:34:43.000 --> 00:34:47.541
Named in 1996, this area isn't just about
cinema, it's also a street food haven.

00:34:48.500 --> 00:34:50.791
The streets are lined with
vendors offering

00:34:50.791 --> 00:34:53.250
every kind of Korean street
food imaginable.

00:34:59.375 --> 00:35:03.291
As we ventured deeper into the old town,
we found ourselves at Gukje Market.

00:35:03.958 --> 00:35:06.125
Gukje means international and was set up

00:35:06.125 --> 00:35:08.791
by post-Korean war refugees
selling smuggled

00:35:09.083 --> 00:35:13.083
and imported goods which laid the foundations
for the current Gukje Market.

00:35:13.750 --> 00:35:16.958
You find everything from street food,
machinery tools to kitchenware.

00:35:23.500 --> 00:35:26.125
Not far from Gukje, we make our
way to the Busan Tower.

00:35:27.000 --> 00:35:30.041
Built in 1973, as a symbol for Busan's

00:35:30.041 --> 00:35:33.291
future development and prosperity,
the tower rises

00:35:33.291 --> 00:35:35.833
120 meters above the nearby park.

00:35:36.625 --> 00:35:40.208
Here you'll find locals engaging in
games of Korean chess and go.

00:35:43.708 --> 00:35:45.583
For dinner, we decided to get some pizza

00:35:45.583 --> 00:35:47.416
near our accommodations

00:35:47.416 --> 00:35:48.916
and visited the Sol Tap House.

00:35:49.750 --> 00:35:51.041
It was great to have 
a little break from

00:35:51.041 --> 00:35:53.208
all the Korean food, 
and the pizzas here

00:35:53.208 --> 00:35:54.541
were honestly great.

00:35:55.416 --> 00:35:56.916
They were so good that we
actually ordered

00:35:56.916 --> 00:35:59.375
takeaway on one of the separate
nights here.

00:36:03.125 --> 00:36:05.500
After dinner, we head 
down to Gwangalli beach

00:36:05.500 --> 00:36:08.041
and find this very interesting, 
slow mailbox.

00:36:08.666 --> 00:36:10.041
Essentially, you can write a letter and

00:36:10.041 --> 00:36:12.208
have it arrive in about a year's time.

00:36:12.750 --> 00:36:14.541
I found it to be a quirky little activity

00:36:14.541 --> 00:36:17.333
and it was free of charge, 
so why not write one?

00:36:19.666 --> 00:36:21.125
Afterwards we spent the rest of the

00:36:21.125 --> 00:36:23.500
evening enjoying the view of
the Gwanggan Bridge.

00:36:24.750 --> 00:36:26.750
Both from the beach and from
our accommodation.

00:36:30.916 --> 00:36:32.875
For more things to do, check
out the following.

00:36:52.125 --> 00:36:53.750
For our second day in Busan, 

00:36:53.750 --> 00:36:56.791
We booked tickets for the 
Haeundae Blueline Sky Capsules.

00:37:00.208 --> 00:37:02.125
This 30 minute journey,
drifting from Mipo

00:37:02.125 --> 00:37:05.250
to Cheongsapo and about 10
meters above the ground

00:37:05.625 --> 00:37:08.291
offers views of the ocean
and the coastal landscapes.

00:37:14.166 --> 00:37:17.375
It's the type of unique experience that
makes you fall in love with Busan.

00:37:23.083 --> 00:37:27.416
We get off at the Cheongsapo station and make
our way to the nearby observatory.

00:37:27.791 --> 00:37:31.916
However it was too windy when we were there
so they had to close off access to it.

00:37:38.083 --> 00:37:39.666
We continued by strolling
along the coastal

00:37:39.666 --> 00:37:42.708
road until we found ourselves
at this seafood restaurant

00:37:43.333 --> 00:37:46.250
We ordered a set of abalone
ramyun, a dish

00:37:46.250 --> 00:37:48.500
that perfectly marries the
briny freshness

00:37:48.625 --> 00:37:52.541
of the sea with the comforting warmth
of the spicy noodle soup.

00:38:14.041 --> 00:38:15.791
As we head back to 
Cheongsapo station,

00:38:16.166 --> 00:38:18.708
we caught a glimpse of 
the Haeundae Blueline train

00:38:18.708 --> 00:38:20.000
as it crosses the street.

00:38:24.583 --> 00:38:27.958
It's a rather popular spot for photos
thanks to social media.

00:38:31.833 --> 00:38:33.958
Instead of hopping back on the train to Mipo

00:38:34.291 --> 00:38:35.666
we opted for the scenic route,

00:38:36.000 --> 00:38:37.416
following the Moontan Road.

00:38:39.083 --> 00:38:43.666
Moontan translates to "Moonlight Walk" and
is a trail where visitors can enjoy the

00:38:43.708 --> 00:38:45.958
full glow of the moonlight as
they walk at night.

00:38:47.125 --> 00:38:48.416
During the day however, you're provided

00:38:48.416 --> 00:38:50.541
with views of the passing
sky capsules

00:38:50.750 --> 00:38:51.833
and the ocean.

00:38:54.916 --> 00:38:58.500
It's a very easy trail to do so I highly
recommend it if you're up for the walk.

00:39:19.250 --> 00:39:20.750
We make our way to Haeundae Beach,

00:39:21.208 --> 00:39:24.208
arguably the most famous 
stretch of sand in Busan

00:39:31.708 --> 00:39:33.291
We take a moment to soak in the beach

00:39:33.291 --> 00:39:36.500
scenery and watch as the sun
sets over the horizon,

00:39:36.791 --> 00:39:38.791
casting a golden glow over the area.

00:39:42.541 --> 00:39:44.875
Before leaving,
we stop at the Tiger Gelatteok.

00:39:45.666 --> 00:39:48.625
A place that serves rice cakes 
filled with Italian gelato.

00:39:49.375 --> 00:39:51.250
This gelato comes in a box with six

00:39:51.250 --> 00:39:53.458
different flavors, perfect for a family,

00:39:53.708 --> 00:39:55.291
but a bit much 
just for the two of us.

00:39:55.666 --> 00:39:57.791
No worries though, 
we stash the extras in

00:39:57.791 --> 00:39:59.458
our freezer for another time.

00:40:07.000 --> 00:40:08.250
Here are more things to do in the area.

00:40:21.750 --> 00:40:22.791
The next morning,

00:40:22.791 --> 00:40:25.416
we head to the 
Haedong Yonggungsa Temple,

00:40:25.416 --> 00:40:27.583
also known as the Dragon Palace.

00:40:33.000 --> 00:40:34.750
It's a stunning seaside Buddhist temple

00:40:34.750 --> 00:40:37.625
perched on rocky cliffs right
above the sea.

00:40:39.000 --> 00:40:41.541
What makes the temple unique is its rare

00:40:41.541 --> 00:40:45.333
coastal location as most Korean
temples are located near mountains.

00:41:19.250 --> 00:41:21.625
Next, we take the bus back,
heading towards

00:41:21.625 --> 00:41:24.458
Gwangalli, but make a stop
at the Museum 1.

00:41:28.583 --> 00:41:31.750
It's a media art museum 
established in 2019.

00:41:32.625 --> 00:41:35.791
Inside we find around 
100 contemporary artworks,

00:41:36.333 --> 00:41:38.416
from media installations
and video art

00:41:38.666 --> 00:41:41.875
by 21 leading Korean and international
artists.

00:42:06.208 --> 00:42:08.416
We make our way 
back to Gwangalli Beach,

00:42:08.875 --> 00:42:11.416
just in time to see the bridge light up.

00:42:31.625 --> 00:42:33.416
If you happen to visit 
Gwangalli on a weekend,

00:42:33.833 --> 00:42:36.458
then keep an eye out for 
the weekly drone show display

00:42:36.625 --> 00:42:39.333
held every Saturday 
at 8pm and 10pm.

00:42:40.208 --> 00:42:42.583
It's a modern spectacle 
against the night sky

00:42:42.750 --> 00:42:45.375
adding a touch of magic 
to the beach experience.

00:42:54.583 --> 00:42:56.791
Here are a few more things 
to do around the area.

00:43:07.875 --> 00:43:12.291
For our final day in Busan, we head to
the Gamcheon Culture Village.

00:43:17.125 --> 00:43:19.916
This colorful village is perched
on a steep hillside.

00:43:20.625 --> 00:43:23.041
It's a vibrant splash of color and life,

00:43:23.458 --> 00:43:25.958
which stands in stark contrast
to the bleak

00:43:25.958 --> 00:43:27.250
past of the village.

00:43:28.458 --> 00:43:32.208
Gamcheon was originally settled by war
refugees from across the country.

00:43:32.833 --> 00:43:36.083
But in 2009, students, artists
and residents

00:43:36.083 --> 00:43:38.708
decorated the village, transforming
the village

00:43:38.708 --> 00:43:39.791
into what it is today.

00:43:42.041 --> 00:43:43.791
We visit this cafe for some drinks, but

00:43:43.791 --> 00:43:46.375
primarily for the panoramic
view of the village.

00:43:56.958 --> 00:44:00.250
While exploring, we stumble upon
a photo flipbook store.

00:44:01.375 --> 00:44:04.458
It's a quirky little shop where you can
create your own photo flipbook.

00:44:08.416 --> 00:44:12.041
You'll find a selection of props you can use,
and the staff is incredibly helpful,

00:44:12.625 --> 00:44:15.666
offering tips and guidance on
poses and what to do.

00:44:16.000 --> 00:44:17.625
Not only does this make for a fantastic

00:44:17.625 --> 00:44:20.708
souvenir, but it's also a unique
and fun experience

00:44:21.041 --> 00:44:22.916
that I wholeheartedly recommend.

00:44:27.416 --> 00:44:30.666
Afterwards, we make a stop at this
bakery for a quick snack.

00:44:57.750 --> 00:44:59.750
Arguably the most famous spot
in the village,

00:45:00.250 --> 00:45:04.375
the Stairs to See the Stars
is a steep 148-step staircase

00:45:05.083 --> 00:45:06.958
It was used by villagers returning home

00:45:06.958 --> 00:45:09.666
from the market who jokingly
proclaimed it was

00:45:09.666 --> 00:45:13.000
so exhausting you'd see stars by the
time you reached the top.

00:45:19.583 --> 00:45:22.500
We leave the village behind and
make our way to Seomyeon.

00:45:25.291 --> 00:45:27.416
We start by exploring the
Jeonpo Cafe Street,

00:45:28.000 --> 00:45:30.458
a paradise for cafe enthusiasts
with stylish

00:45:30.458 --> 00:45:33.041
and aesthetic cafes on nearly
every corner.

00:45:56.916 --> 00:45:59.208
Next, we decide to test our skills

00:45:59.458 --> 00:46:02.166
and visited the Running Man 
experience in Busan

00:46:02.916 --> 00:46:04.625
It's an interactive game attraction

00:46:04.625 --> 00:46:08.708
inspired by the popular Korean
variety show Running Man

00:46:08.875 --> 00:46:11.708
Test yourself with a series of 
games and challenges

00:46:11.708 --> 00:46:13.000
straight out of the tv show,

00:46:13.375 --> 00:46:15.166
and for those with 
a competitive streak,

00:46:15.291 --> 00:46:19.083
there's leaderboards to conquer 
and various difficulty levels to tackle.

00:46:19.583 --> 00:46:21.000
Initially, I thought it might be a bit

00:46:21.000 --> 00:46:22.875
gimmicky, but it turned out to
be one of my favorite

00:46:22.958 --> 00:46:24.250
experiences in Busan.

00:46:24.916 --> 00:46:27.875
If you're a fan of the show, then this
is an absolute must-visit.

00:46:31.500 --> 00:46:33.291
After burning off some calories, we were

00:46:33.291 --> 00:46:35.958
starting to get hungry, so in
search for dinner, we

00:46:35.958 --> 00:46:37.666
head down to the Pojangmacha Street.

00:46:39.291 --> 00:46:44.041
You'll find rows of glowing orange tents serving
up Busan's boldest street food, 

00:46:44.500 --> 00:46:46.708
From spicy tteokbokki and grilled eel

00:46:46.875 --> 00:46:49.416
to soju-fueled conversations with locals

00:46:49.750 --> 00:46:53.250
this is where you get a glimpse 
of the very soul of Busan.

00:47:04.333 --> 00:47:06.500
Another gem, I want to mention is 

00:47:06.500 --> 00:47:08.208
Gijang Son Kalguksu

00:47:08.791 --> 00:47:12.333
A popular no-frills 
hole in the wall noodle shop.

00:47:12.583 --> 00:47:17.000
where you can even witness the noodles
being hand pulled just right outside.

00:47:17.375 --> 00:47:19.583
The star of the show 
is their Son Kalguksu

00:47:19.875 --> 00:47:22.416
thick, chewy noodles, swimming in a

00:47:22.416 --> 00:47:24.208
rich, achovy based broth.

00:47:36.041 --> 00:47:39.500
We finish the evening, 
by exploring the lively Seomyeon.

00:47:54.083 --> 00:47:56.791
For more things to do in Busan,
consider the following.

00:48:12.041 --> 00:48:13.750
After ending our time in Busan,

00:48:13.750 --> 00:48:15.291
we head to the airport

00:48:15.291 --> 00:48:17.500
to catch a direct flight to Jeju Island.

00:48:25.500 --> 00:48:30.375
Jeju Island is a place of raw, untamed
beauty with deep cultural roots.

00:48:31.208 --> 00:48:32.916
It's a place where you can
get lost in the

00:48:32.916 --> 00:48:35.416
breathtaking beauty of nature
and then reconnect

00:48:35.833 --> 00:48:38.000
with the intricate weave of
local traditions.

00:48:38.833 --> 00:48:41.166
Compared to Seoul and Busan,
this volcanic

00:48:41.166 --> 00:48:43.666
island feels like stepping
into a different world.

00:48:44.166 --> 00:48:46.500
A world that moves at its own pace.

00:48:49.333 --> 00:48:52.583
We arrive at the airport and immediately
pick up a rental car.

00:48:53.166 --> 00:48:56.041
We opted for an EV, the Hyundai IONIQ 5,

00:48:56.291 --> 00:48:58.416
that served us well during
our Jeju adventures.

00:49:01.000 --> 00:49:04.458
When renting a car in Jeju Island, there's
a couple of things to be aware of.

00:49:05.666 --> 00:49:09.208
I highly recommend booking your car in advance
to lock in the cheaper rates.

00:49:10.041 --> 00:49:13.291
Most cars come with built-in GPS with
integration with Naver Map.

00:49:14.416 --> 00:49:16.750
Gas-driven cars are usually
much cheaper than

00:49:16.750 --> 00:49:19.833
EVs, but if you decide to
go with an EV, then

00:49:19.833 --> 00:49:21.791
you'll find plenty of charging
stations around

00:49:21.791 --> 00:49:24.041
the island, and depending on
the rental company,

00:49:24.375 --> 00:49:26.333
they might even provide you
with a charging card

00:49:26.333 --> 00:49:29.208
that you could use to
charge your EV free of charge.

00:49:32.208 --> 00:49:34.416
Driving on Jeju Island is relatively easy

00:49:34.416 --> 00:49:36.291
compared to the major cities
such as Seoul

00:49:36.291 --> 00:49:38.541
and Busan, but here are a couple of tips.

00:49:39.250 --> 00:49:40.958
There are strict speed limits
on the island

00:49:40.958 --> 00:49:43.375
with plenty of hidden speed
cameras, so be

00:49:43.375 --> 00:49:44.250
sure to pay attention.

00:49:45.166 --> 00:49:47.250
Right turns on red are allowed in Jeju

00:49:47.250 --> 00:49:49.666
Island, which are something I
needed to get used to.

00:49:50.125 --> 00:49:52.750
Traffic is generally light outside of Jeju City

00:49:52.750 --> 00:49:54.416
which makes driving on the island 

00:49:54.416 --> 00:49:56.291
manageable even for beginners.

00:49:58.916 --> 00:50:02.250
Overall, driving on Jeju Island is pretty
easy and straightforward.

00:50:03.083 --> 00:50:04.916
It's also the best way to explore since

00:50:04.916 --> 00:50:07.458
public transportation on the
island is limited.

00:50:10.791 --> 00:50:15.416
We decided to stay in Jeju City and booked
a room at the Grand Hyatt Jeju.

00:50:18.833 --> 00:50:23.083
This five-star hotel comes with all the
luxury amenities you'd expect.

00:50:26.791 --> 00:50:28.958
A major plus for us was the EV charging

00:50:28.958 --> 00:50:31.750
stations down at the parking
basement, which made it

00:50:31.750 --> 00:50:34.083
easy for us to charge 
our rental car overnight.

00:50:40.583 --> 00:50:42.083
Depending on your room, you might even

00:50:42.083 --> 00:50:44.875
catch a view of the airplanes
gliding in towards

00:50:45.000 --> 00:50:45.916
the nearby airport.

00:50:50.250 --> 00:50:52.125
We decide to head down to Dodu-dong, 

00:50:52.375 --> 00:50:53.750
The Rainbow Coastal Road.

00:50:55.916 --> 00:50:57.958
It's a vibrant and colorful coastal road

00:50:57.958 --> 00:51:00.625
known for its rainbow-colored wall 
and ocean views.

00:51:03.750 --> 00:51:05.375
Local residents had long expressed their

00:51:05.375 --> 00:51:07.291
desire to liven out the plane protected

00:51:07.291 --> 00:51:09.333
walls along the coastal road, 
which was

00:51:09.333 --> 00:51:11.375
initially installed 
to prevent cars from

00:51:11.375 --> 00:51:12.333
skidding off the edge.

00:51:12.750 --> 00:51:15.000
What began as a safety measure 
evolved

00:51:15.000 --> 00:51:17.250
into a colorful landmark 
of Jeju Island.

00:51:22.458 --> 00:51:25.000
Not too far from Dodu-dong, 
we stumble upon

00:51:25.000 --> 00:51:28.166
a pair of red and white 
horse-shaped lighthouses

00:51:28.166 --> 00:51:30.125
standing proudly at the edge of a port.

00:51:38.125 --> 00:51:40.166
Next, we head to the Abebe Bakery.

00:51:42.416 --> 00:51:44.583
Here you'll find these cream-filled
donuts,

00:51:44.958 --> 00:51:47.208
which comes in different flavors
and toppings.

00:51:50.583 --> 00:51:52.833
Having difficulty in deciding
on what to get,

00:51:53.250 --> 00:51:56.041
we end up buying a whole box,
saving the rest

00:51:56.166 --> 00:51:56.750
for later.

00:52:07.500 --> 00:52:09.708
In the evening, we made our
way to Dongmun Market.

00:52:11.166 --> 00:52:13.166
Dongmun has been the heartbeat of Jeju's

00:52:13.166 --> 00:52:16.541
local food scene since 1945,
and as soon as

00:52:16.541 --> 00:52:18.666
you step inside, you'll understand why.

00:52:19.166 --> 00:52:23.333
The narrow alleys are packed with vendors
enticing you with sizzling street food.

00:52:23.708 --> 00:52:26.375
The smells are overwhelming in
the best way possible.

00:52:26.875 --> 00:52:28.416
There's no escaping the pull of it.

00:52:29.500 --> 00:52:31.291
It's also in the market where we find the

00:52:31.291 --> 00:52:33.166
Young Handsome Men lobsters,

00:52:33.166 --> 00:52:36.750
where eligible young bachelors 
charm you with K-pop dance moves 

00:52:37.083 --> 00:52:38.666
while serving up grilled lobster.

00:52:47.208 --> 00:52:49.291
Just your regular lobster

00:52:49.291 --> 00:52:50.666
not anything special, 

00:52:50.666 --> 00:52:52.583
but I'm all there for the show.

00:52:52.583 --> 00:52:53.416
The show was awesome

00:52:53.416 --> 00:52:55.541
the guys showed a lot of showmanship,

00:52:55.541 --> 00:52:58.083
5 out of 10 for the lobster

00:52:58.083 --> 00:52:59.291
and 10 out of 10

00:52:59.291 --> 00:53:00.666
for the showmanship.

00:53:00.958 --> 00:53:04.000
Of course, after some food,

00:53:04.000 --> 00:53:06.208
we're topping it off with some local

00:53:06.208 --> 00:53:08.416
halabong tangerine juice

00:53:08.875 --> 00:53:11.000
freshly extracted from 
the shop right over here.

00:53:26.833 --> 00:53:29.166
On our second day in Jeju,
we made our way

00:53:29.166 --> 00:53:31.666
to the eastern side of the
island to visit

00:53:31.833 --> 00:53:35.250
Seongsan Ilchulbong, also
known as Sunrise Peak.

00:53:36.833 --> 00:53:41.666
It's a 5,000-year-old volcanic crater that
rises dramatically from the sea.

00:53:44.833 --> 00:53:49.041
It's famous for its view of the sunrise, which
is why so many people wake up at an

00:53:49.041 --> 00:53:50.916
ungodly hour to make the climb.

00:53:51.375 --> 00:53:54.833
We didn't quite manage that, and honestly,
I  kinda wish we had.

00:53:55.125 --> 00:53:58.708
And the hike to the summit? A short
incline of just 20 to 30 minutes.

00:54:07.083 --> 00:54:12.333
We make our way down to meet the legendary
Inu Jeju's famous sea woman.

00:54:15.458 --> 00:54:19.333
These incredible women have been diving with
breathing equipment for centuries,

00:54:19.583 --> 00:54:21.833
harvesting seafood straight
from the ocean floor.

00:54:22.625 --> 00:54:25.875
For these women, this isn't just
a job, it's a way of life.

00:54:27.083 --> 00:54:29.291
There's a daily show that's
part singing and

00:54:29.291 --> 00:54:31.833
part dancing, but don't expect
too much from it.

00:54:32.291 --> 00:54:34.958
Afterward, the women dive
into the sea, and

00:54:34.958 --> 00:54:36.625
you can actually buy whatever
they catch,

00:54:37.000 --> 00:54:39.416
and have it prepared for you
at a nearby restaurant.

00:54:54.000 --> 00:54:56.875
Next, we make a quick stop
at the Gwangchigi beach

00:54:57.666 --> 00:54:59.416
known for its expansive
tidal flats,

00:54:59.875 --> 00:55:03.083
black volcanic rocks, and the view
of Seongsan Ilchulbong.

00:55:04.833 --> 00:55:09.916
During low tide, the beach reveals moss-covered
rocks and shallow tidal pools,

00:55:10.375 --> 00:55:14.416
hosting small creatures like tiny crabs,
snails, and shellfish.

00:55:24.958 --> 00:55:28.000
A need for some caffeine,
we stop by Cafe Orrrn.

00:55:29.958 --> 00:55:33.583
This place has the kind of minimalist, sleek
design you'd expect to find in a

00:55:33.583 --> 00:55:36.541
trendy city, not on the coast of
a volcanic island.

00:55:36.958 --> 00:55:38.375
But that's the beauty of Jeju.

00:55:38.875 --> 00:55:41.250
The cafe's sharp lines and
modern architecture

00:55:41.250 --> 00:55:44.083
blends perfectly with the rugged
coastline outside,

00:55:44.625 --> 00:55:47.333
a perfect stop after a morning
of hiking and exploring.

00:55:57.416 --> 00:56:01.291
For a nearby optional activity, 
Bunder Des Lumieres is a former

00:56:01.291 --> 00:56:04.708
military bunker that has been turned
into a digital art museum.

00:56:06.541 --> 00:56:10.375
Inside, you'll find high-definition
projections of famous artworks.

00:56:25.208 --> 00:56:28.500
However, I would recommend spending your
time at the Snoopy Garden.

00:56:30.583 --> 00:56:32.833
It's amusing in all the right ways, like

00:56:32.833 --> 00:56:35.666
stepping into the mind of 
Charles Schulz himself,

00:56:36.083 --> 00:56:40.000
where Snoopy, Charlie Brown, and the rest
of the gang live out their endless,

00:56:40.000 --> 00:56:43.541
existential crisis against a backdrop
of colorful exhibits.

00:56:44.000 --> 00:56:46.083
The garden is beautifully themed, and the

00:56:46.083 --> 00:56:47.958
whole atmosphere is surprisingly
charming.

00:57:04.208 --> 00:57:06.250
I'll admit, I'm not the biggest Snoopy

00:57:06.250 --> 00:57:08.375
fan, but even I found the
whole thing amusing.

00:57:11.000 --> 00:57:15.333
So if you're a die-hard Snoopy fan, then
let me be blunt. You need to visit.

00:57:35.833 --> 00:57:38.333
To finish the day, we make our
way to Seopjikoji.

00:57:39.041 --> 00:57:41.833
Famous for featuring in several
Korean dramas,

00:57:41.833 --> 00:57:45.541
it's a stunning stretch of coastline
where volcanic rock

00:57:45.541 --> 00:57:49.041
formations meet the deep blue waters
of the East China Sea.

00:57:51.916 --> 00:57:55.833
A highlight of the area is the lighthouse
that sits at the top of a hill.

00:58:09.208 --> 00:58:13.250
Climbing up to it rewards you with an unbeatable
view of the nearby coastline.

00:58:29.833 --> 00:58:33.750
On our third day in Jeju, we start
by visiting the Hueree Park.

00:58:36.000 --> 00:58:38.625
Known for the season of flower
displays, visitors can

00:58:38.625 --> 00:58:41.291
experience the varied flower
seasons of Jeju Island.

00:58:43.083 --> 00:58:46.208
During autumn, you can expect to see
the Pink Muhly grass gardens.

00:58:48.500 --> 00:58:51.541
While in spring, hydrangeas dominate
the landscape.

00:59:12.375 --> 00:59:15.208
There's even a small pig farm
experience. It's

00:59:15.208 --> 00:59:17.250
part of the mini animal farm
within the park.

00:59:18.291 --> 00:59:20.875
Here you can interact with and
feed the black Jeju pigs.

00:59:39.666 --> 00:59:41.375
It's time for some waterfalls.

00:59:41.875 --> 00:59:43.500
The first to be the Jeongbang waterfall.

00:59:53.666 --> 00:59:55.041
It's one of the few waterfalls
in the world,

00:59:55.416 --> 00:59:57.208
where the water tumbles directly 
into the sea.

00:59:58.125 --> 01:00:00.208
Later we found ourselves at
the Cheonjiyeon waterfall

01:00:00.666 --> 01:00:03.791
arguably the most famous
waterfall in Jeju Island.

01:00:11.583 --> 01:00:13.291
Next, we visit the Oedolgae,

01:00:13.666 --> 01:00:17.666
a volcanic sea stack rising about 20 meters
from the southern part of Jeju.

01:00:18.250 --> 01:00:20.416
Its name literally means "lonely rock".

01:00:25.250 --> 01:00:26.666
Next up is Gamttanam,

01:00:27.208 --> 01:00:29.583
a tangerine-themed cafe and orchid.

01:00:30.541 --> 01:00:34.375
The cafe sits beside a tangerine orchid
run by a family for generations.

01:00:35.958 --> 01:00:38.458
During autumn and winter, you can
pick your own tangerines,

01:00:39.000 --> 01:00:40.875
tools, baskets, and weighing included

01:00:46.666 --> 01:00:50.833
At the small cafe, you can sip on house
favorites like the fresh halabong juice

01:00:52.666 --> 01:00:55.833
and taste desserts, such as
the tangerine mousse cake.

01:01:09.791 --> 01:01:13.666
For dinner, we decided to dine in
an order some room service.

01:01:26.666 --> 01:01:28.708
We begin our final day in Jeju 

01:01:29.500 --> 01:01:31.708
by visiting the Arte Museum.

01:01:32.875 --> 01:01:37.041
Arguably the most impressive digital art museum
I've come across during this trip.

01:01:42.666 --> 01:01:46.166
The digital art displays are both unique
and visually impressive.

01:01:47.958 --> 01:01:50.916
The museum features a variety
of exhibitions

01:01:51.333 --> 01:01:54.083
that aims to transport you into
visually stunning realms.

01:02:24.666 --> 01:02:28.000
We head to Saebil, a cafe housed in
an abandoned hotel resort.

01:02:28.625 --> 01:02:31.583
It features a large interior space,
with plenty of seating,

01:02:32.166 --> 01:02:34.583
and a large variety of big
goods and beverages.

01:02:38.666 --> 01:02:42.708
The cafe also features an outdoor area,
which is full of pink muhly grass,

01:02:43.083 --> 01:02:45.666
creating the perfect backdrop, awesome
photos, and detail.

01:02:48.208 --> 01:02:50.666
We also make a quick stop
by the lonely tree,

01:02:50.791 --> 01:02:51.875
not too far from the cafe.

01:02:56.666 --> 01:02:58.791
We then head to the Osulloc Tea Museum,

01:02:59.291 --> 01:03:03.666
a small museum dedicated to rich
history of Korean tea.

01:03:14.666 --> 01:03:18.541
There's also a large outdoor space, which
features a beautiful green tea field.

01:03:40.791 --> 01:03:43.750
Within the museum grounds, you can
find an innisfree store,

01:03:44.125 --> 01:03:45.583
a well-known Korean skincarebrand.

01:03:53.250 --> 01:03:55.416
There's also a cafe where
you can sample

01:03:55.416 --> 01:03:58.166
Osulloc's various teas 
and tea-flavored dessert.

01:04:00.791 --> 01:04:05.541
And finally, we spend our remaining time
at the Sinchang Windmill Coastal Road

01:04:06.041 --> 01:04:10.208
A scenic coastal path known for its stunning
coastal views and iconic windmills.

01:04:27.125 --> 01:04:29.625
The coastal road is known for its
spectacular sunsets,

01:04:30.000 --> 01:04:33.083
as the sun dips below the horizon, 
the sky transforms

01:04:33.083 --> 01:04:34.708
into a canvas of vibrant colors.

01:04:35.291 --> 01:04:38.333
Many flock to the spot in the evening
to capture the stunning views.

01:04:56.000 --> 01:05:00.208
We personally found it to be
the perfect way to end our time in Jeju.

01:05:01.541 --> 01:05:06.000
If you want a more exciting or fun 
way to finish your time in Jeju

01:05:06.208 --> 01:05:09.208
Then consider spending 
the day at 9.81 Park

01:05:09.541 --> 01:05:12.250
Korea's first ever non-motorized 
racing theme park,

01:05:12.666 --> 01:05:15.875
that offer visitors the chance 
to experience gravity racing,

01:05:16.083 --> 01:05:19.125
which allows you to race in gokarts 
with help of gravity

01:05:31.250 --> 01:05:34.041
For more things to do in Jeju, 
check out the following.

01:05:45.666 --> 01:05:49.166
Before wrapping things up, let's quickly
break down the budget for this trip.

01:05:50.000 --> 01:05:54.166
Our flights from Copenhagen to South Korea,
including domestic flights to and from

01:05:54.166 --> 01:05:57.916
Jeju Island, came to around
1,925 US dollars.

01:05:58.875 --> 01:06:03.541
Accommodation costs total of about 2,246 US
dollars, but this can be brought down

01:06:03.541 --> 01:06:05.291
if you opt for more budget-friendly stays.

01:06:06.541 --> 01:06:12.333
In total, the trip cost us approximately
5,521 US dollars for two people.

01:06:14.666 --> 01:06:17.958
Alright, so that was how to spend
14 days in South Korea.

01:06:18.666 --> 01:06:21.750
Yet again, if you want a written version 
of all this, be sure to check out

01:06:21.750 --> 01:06:23.541
my South Korea travel guide, 

01:06:23.541 --> 01:06:26.000
where I go into much more details 
about the trip,

01:06:26.250 --> 01:06:30.291
including activities, cafes, and restaurants
that didn't make it into this video.

01:06:30.875 --> 01:06:34.541
It's designed to help you get the most out
of your time in South Korea, and if

01:06:34.541 --> 01:06:36.458
you'd like to support me and
the channel directly,

01:06:36.875 --> 01:06:39.166
grabbing a copy of the guide is
the best way to do it.

01:06:40.625 --> 01:06:43.375
Overall, I had an incredible time
in South Korea,

01:06:43.541 --> 01:06:46.375
and I hope this video inspires you to
take your very own trip.

01:06:46.666 --> 01:06:48.583
This is Allan, safe travels out there,

01:06:48.583 --> 01:06:50.208
and I'll see you guys soon.

